From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Renê de Souza Pinto <rene@renesp.com.br>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vfio/igd: hold the AUX and DDI display power wells on too

Extends the power-well clamp (patch 19) from the main PWR_WELL_CTL_DRIVER
register to the AUX (0x45444) and DDI (0x45454) DRIVER-copy registers, which
gate the AUX-channel and DDI/PHY blocks of the display engine.

Patch 19 stopped the input-driven runtime freeze (main wells PW1-PWD). A
separate freeze appears on Windows VM reboot/power-off: the guest unloads its
display driver and tears the whole display down, which powers down the AUX and
DDI wells as well - wells patch 19 does not hold. An asynchronous access to a
register behind one of those while it is off or mid-transition wedges the host
the same way.

Same request/state bit layout and the same BAR0 page (0x45000) as the main
register, so this reuses igd_pwr_well_ops and adds no new vmexits: on each
guest write, currently-requested wells are OR'd back in so a well never drops.

CAVEAT: unlike the main and AUX wells (holding them on only costs idle power),
the DDI wells drive the port PHY, which the driver expects to power-cycle when
it re-trains the link on the next boot. Holding them on can leave the display
black after a guest reboot. Verify the display returns after a reboot with this
applied; if it does not, drop 0x45454 from igd_pwr_well_aux_ddi[] and keep AUX
only.

This addresses only the display-teardown path. The other reboot/power-off
trigger - the PCI D3 + function-reset + decode edge - is not trappable in QEMU
and needs the host kernel's vfio-pci settle-window fix.

Signed-off-by: Renê de Souza Pinto <rene@renesp.com.br>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/vfio/igd.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/qemu-xen/hw/vfio/igd.c b/tools/qemu-xen/hw/vfio/igd.c
index c2e5107a44..d3f6218b55 100644
--- a/tools/qemu-xen/hw/vfio/igd.c
+++ b/tools/qemu-xen/hw/vfio/igd.c
@@ -22,6 +22,37 @@
                                             &pwquirk->mem[0], 1);
         QLIST_INSERT_HEAD(&vdev->bars[nr].quirks, pwquirk, next);
     }
+
+    /*
+     * AUX (0x45444) and DDI (0x45454) power-well clamp (gen9+): the DRIVER-copy
+     * registers for the AUX and DDI/PHY wells, same request/state layout and the
+     * same BAR0 page.  A guest tearing the display down at shutdown/reboot powers
+     * these down too, so hold them on with the same accumulate-on logic.
+     *
+     * NOTE: holding DDI/PHY wells on can interfere with port re-training on the
+     * next boot - verify the display returns after a guest reboot; if not, drop
+     * 0x45454 and keep only AUX.
+     */
+    if (gen >= 9) {
+        static const uint32_t igd_pwr_well_aux_ddi[] = { 0x45444, 0x45454 };
+        unsigned k;
+
+        for (k = 0; k < ARRAY_SIZE(igd_pwr_well_aux_ddi); k++) {
+            VFIOQuirk *q = vfio_quirk_alloc(1);
+            IGDPwrWellQuirk *pq = q->data = g_malloc0(sizeof(*pq));
+
+            pq->vdev = vdev;
+            pq->bar = nr;
+            pq->bar_offset = igd_pwr_well_aux_ddi[k];
+            memory_region_init_io(&q->mem[0], OBJECT(vdev),
+                                  &igd_pwr_well_ops, pq,
+                                  "vfio-igd-pwr-well-aux-ddi-quirk", 4);
+            memory_region_add_subregion_overlap(vdev->bars[nr].region.mem,
+                                                igd_pwr_well_aux_ddi[k],
+                                                &q->mem[0], 1);
+            QLIST_INSERT_HEAD(&vdev->bars[nr].quirks, q, next);
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 void vfio_probe_igd_bar4_quirk(VFIOPCIDevice *vdev, int nr)
